  "worked_solution": "To find the additive inverse of the number $9$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(9)=-9.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n9+(-9)=9-9=0\\,✓\n$$",
